From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xorbidden <xorbidden@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:13:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] camera_device: select the stream's camera before the first
 read

The worker read a frame from whatever camera the kernel had last and
only then asked for its own. Switching from the front camera to the
back one therefore started one more front session; on the Mi 9T the
pop-up camera went up and down again for nothing. Send
HAKIOS_CAMERA_SENSOR as soon as the device is open; a driver that
already runs that camera takes it as a no-op.

Tested on the Mi 9T (old port, ddc0ce5): no extra pop-up when
switching cameras.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 userland/src/camera_device.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/userland/src/camera_device.c b/userland/src/camera_device.c
index 24b1d6b..e6aaeb0 100644
--- a/userland/src/camera_device.c
+++ b/userland/src/camera_device.c
@@ -1324,6 +1324,15 @@ worker(void *context)
 		return NULL;
 	}
 	isp_init(&isp);
+	{
+		/*
+		 * This stream's camera asked for before the first read: else the first frames come from the kernel's last
+		 * camera, which is started for them (on the Mi 9T the front one pops up and down again for nothing)
+		 */
+		struct hakios_camera_command c = { .command = HAKIOS_CAMERA_SENSOR, .a = s->camera->sensor, .b = ~0u };
+
+		(void)write(device, &c, sizeof(c));
+	}
 	while (s->running && failures < 5) {
 		ssize_t n;
 
